      <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>you are planning a full retrofit which will take care of most of the air leakage </airSeal>
                <mainWalls>I modeled with R15 foam retrofit to get rebates , but R20 foam is a safer wall system</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>I brought the ceiling value to R60</ceilings>
                <exposedFloors>add same amount to exposed floors as you install on walls, consider pulling plywood off and refreshing the insulation first</exposedFloors>
                <foundation>add at least R15 to the basement walls</foundation>
                <windows>install new energy star triple glazed 2x low e windows</windows>
                <doors>install new doors</doors>
                <VentilationSystem>once you lower the air leakage this house should have an HRV</VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>it is worth upgrading the furnace to electric or new high efficiecy oil.  mini split heat pumps are worth looking into</HeatingSystem>
                <AdditionalComments>be sure to check the energy solutions website for the most up to date rebate  information</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
      <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="false" evaluationCost="">
